    "caption": "Prepare a light dinner and take it to the next level with the help of Alianca Casal Mendes Rosé. Sometimes, all you need to make a meal more memorable is a good glass of wine.\n\nMake this Asparagus Salad in under 30 minutes with some greens, soft-boiled eggs, and prosciutto. The dressing comes in the form of a beurre blanc, whose sweetness and tang balance out the salty prosciutto and the delicate asparagus harmoniously. Pop open a bottle of rosé to go with the meal. Bursting with notes of berries and melons (perfect for the prosciutto!), grab a bottle of Alianca Casal Mendes Rosé at #TheMarketplace along with all the ingredients that you need to make this Asparagus salad.\nServing Time: 20 minutes\nYield: 4-6 servings\nTip: Serve with Alianca Casal Mendes Rosé.\nIngredients\nFor the Salad:\n1 bunch asparagus, trimmed\n2 cups mixed greens of choice\n4 soft-boiled eggs\n6-8 pcs. prosciutto\nFor the Beurre Blanc:\n1 cup cold butter, cubed\n½ cup dry white wine\n¼ cup white wine vinegar\n½ tbsp. finely chopped shallots\nSalt to taste\n\nProcedure\n1. Blanch asparagus in a pot of boiling salted water for 1 min. Cool in an ice bath. Drain and pat dry.\n2. For the beurre blanc, boil wine, vinegar, and shallots in a saucepan over high heat. Cook until reduced, then whisk in cubes of cold butter on low heat. Season to taste.\n3. To assemble, toss blanched asparagus, mixed greens, soft-boiled eggs, and prosciutto in a bowl. Serve with the beurre blanc and pair with Alianca Casal Mendes Rosé.\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
