    "caption": "Easy, flavorful, and delicious, cook this Shrimp & Chorizo Flatbread for a cozy indoor dinner with friends, and make the occasion even more special by opening a bottle of Beronia Reserva Rioja.\n\nRioja leans more on the heavier side. A full-bodied wine with high tannins and bursting with notes of plums and dark berries, it contrasts the peppery chorizo well, and you’ll be surprised at how it also heightens the rich flavor of the shrimp. Thanks to the flatbread, the combination works pretty deliciously. Head over to #TheMarketplace, explore the expansive selection of wines available, and don’t forget to grab a bottle of Beronia Reserva Rioja while you’re there!\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 6-8 servings\nTip: Serve with Beronia Reserva Rioja.\nIngredients\n2 pcs. round flatbread\n2 tbsps. olive oil\n½ cup chorizo sausage\n½ cup shrimp, peeled and deveined\n½ cup shredded mozzarella\n¼ cup cherry tomatoes, thinly sliced\n1 tbsp. chopped fresh parsley\nSalt and pepper to taste\nProcedure\n1. Preheat oven to 200°C. Line a baking tray with parchment.\n2. Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat. Sear chorizo and crumble with a wooden spoon. Set aside. In the same pan, season and cook shrimp until opaque. Set aside.\n3. Slice flatbread into triangles and place on the baking tray. Top with mozzarella, crumbled chorizo, shrimp, cherry tomatoes, and parsley.\n4. Bake for 8-12 mins. or until the cheese has melted. Serve hot and pair with Beronia Reserva Rioja.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
